  "question": {
    "text": "In the figure, the mass of a ball is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> times the mass of the rod. Length of the rod is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The level of ball is the same as rod level. Find out the time taken by the ball to reach at the upper end of the rod.<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0114_d60dd17ae6f4.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.4</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.45</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.25</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>5</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be accelerations of a ball (upward) and rod (downward), respectively.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0114_f47e8345d309.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /><br /><br />Clearly, from the diagram<br /><br /><math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> ...(i)<br /><br />Now, for the ball<br /><br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math> ...(ii)<br /><br />and for the rod, <math><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> ...(iii)<br /><br />On solving equations (i) and (iii), we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>29</mn></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8593;</mo></math> (upward)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>29</mn></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8595;</mo></math> (downward)<br /><br />So, acceleration of ball w.r.t rod <math><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>29</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Now, displacement of ball w.r.t. rod when it reaches the upper end of rod is <math><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></math> .<br /><br />Using the equation of motion,<br /><br /><math><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>29</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>58</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.4</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  }
}